Used here as the only found real-world (non-production) example of the
XTF 2.4 wire encoding (`geom:`-namespaced, lowercase geometry tags,
`ili:bid`/`ili:tid` namespaced attributes) exercising every geometry kind
(COORD, POLYLINE straight/arc, SURFACE, AREA, MULTICOORD, MULTIPOLYLINE,
MULTISURFACE) in one real transfer - not part of `xtf_corpus/`, which is
scratch/untracked and, as of this writing, 100% XTF 2.3 (see the comment
preceding `interlis.xtf.validate._validate_line_attribute`).
